WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.642 --> 00:00:03.400
- [Narrator] This is Allen Dean Foster.

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:04.930
- Hi, I’m Allen Dean Foster.

00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:06.274
- [Narrator] And he is a
Science Fiction Writer.

00:00:06.274 --> 00:00:07.191
- Yes, I am.

00:00:08.098 --> 00:00:09.074
- [Narrator] You might even be familiar

00:00:09.074 --> 00:00:10.194
with one of his books.

00:00:10.194 --> 00:00:13.146
- In 1975, I worked with
George Lucas and wrote

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:15.366
the book version of "Star Wars.” 

00:00:15.366 --> 00:00:16.267
- [Narrator] No way.

00:00:16.267 --> 00:00:17.100
- Yes way.

00:00:19.674 --> 00:00:20.761
(guitar strums)

00:00:20.761 --> 00:00:24.034
- [Narrator] This is Allen
Dean Foster's office.

00:00:24.034 --> 00:00:27.133
This is the view from
Allen Dean Foster's deck.

00:00:27.133 --> 00:00:29.725
This is how Allen Dean
Foster meet George Lucas.

00:00:29.725 --> 00:00:31.043
- They were looking for
someone to do the book

00:00:31.043 --> 00:00:32.993
version of this science fiction film

00:00:32.993 --> 00:00:34.781
that no one knew anything about.

00:00:34.781 --> 00:00:38.614
I was asked by my publisher
if I'd be interested,

00:00:38.614 --> 00:00:39.447
I said yes,

00:00:39.447 --> 00:00:42.005
and that's how the book came to be.

00:00:42.005 --> 00:00:43.628
- [Narrator] It was the
opportunity of a life time,

00:00:43.628 --> 00:00:46.087
but it came with one pretty big caveat.

00:00:46.087 --> 00:00:47.908
- George's name would be on
the cover, and I couldn't

00:00:47.908 --> 00:00:51.047
admit to having ghost written the book.

00:00:51.047 --> 00:00:52.395
(harpsichord music)

00:00:52.395 --> 00:00:54.815
- [Narrator] So he lied, for a long time.

00:00:54.815 --> 00:00:58.278
- So I had to lie to people
faces for twenty years.

00:00:58.278 --> 00:01:00.945
- [Narrator] This is liar
Allen Dean Foster's library.

00:01:00.945 --> 00:01:02.777
He's written a whole
bunch of novelizations.

00:01:02.777 --> 00:01:03.937
- "Star Wars", of course.

00:01:03.937 --> 00:01:05.273
The first three "Alien" films,

00:01:05.273 --> 00:01:07.993
"The Chronicles of Riddick,”
"Clash of the Titans,” and

00:01:07.993 --> 00:01:10.301
most recently "The Force Awakens.”

00:01:10.301 --> 00:01:11.596
- [Narrator] And a lot of other books, too.

00:01:11.596 --> 00:01:15.189
- [Allen Dean Foster] *listing all books*

00:01:15.189 --> 00:01:16.289
- [Narrator] That's maybe
the least interesting

00:01:16.289 --> 00:01:18.197
thing about him.

00:01:18.197 --> 00:01:22.627
- There's secrets that will
forever remain unrevealed.

00:01:22.627 --> 00:01:24.827
(hard rock guitar music)

00:01:24.827 --> 00:01:25.660
- [Narrator] These are Allen Dean Foster's

00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:27.905
weight-lifting trophies.

00:01:27.905 --> 00:01:29.854
This is Allen Dean Foster's bench press.

00:01:29.854 --> 00:01:30.687
- Okay.

00:01:33.063 --> 00:01:34.811
- [Narrator] Here's Allen
Dean Foster's front kick.

00:01:34.811 --> 00:01:36.422
- Got that from Chuck Norris.

00:01:36.422 --> 00:01:37.537
- [Narrator] Not a joke.

00:01:37.537 --> 00:01:40.158
(upbeat orchestral music)

00:01:40.158 --> 00:01:42.639
Here's Allen Dean Foster with his camera.

00:01:42.639 --> 00:01:46.306
He's recorded his travels
on six continents.

00:01:47.519 --> 00:01:49.890
- I'm stuck on this one
planet that I'm determined

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:53.140
to see as much of it as I possibly can.

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:55.310
- [Narrator] So, how does a world famous,

00:01:55.310 --> 00:01:56.268
crazy prolific,

00:01:56.268 --> 00:01:57.636
sci-fi writer manage to keep this up,

00:01:57.636 --> 00:01:59.808
and still find time for his writing?

00:01:59.808 --> 00:02:02.264
- Well, to stop learning
is to start to die.

00:02:02.264 --> 00:02:04.133
- [Narrator] Didn't
Desiderius Erasmus say that?

00:02:04.133 --> 00:02:05.216
- Yes he did.

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:07.892
(upbeat chamber music)

00:02:07.892 --> 00:02:11.475
- You know, John Ford
only needed one take.

